s area's 405. **Item API:** `/api/v1/items/:id` adds `commands` (`{ name, usage, description }` for each command that applies in the item's current state, from the same table and rule as the comment footer, `commandsFor`, `/help` last) and `replies` (the item's stored requests, oldest first, the newest 50: `{ seq, command, created_at, handled_at, refusal }`; `command` and `refusal` pass the `Withholder`; the note is never returned). They read a new store method, `listAppCommandRequestsForItem` (no schema change). Every other GET response is unchanged. The server still binds only `127.0.0.1`.
